C code built by crates
----------------------
Crates that compile C or assembly into the binary ship that code's licence
with their sources; its notices are part of the crate's entries below when
the crate's package carries them:

- libmimalloc-sys: mimalloc (MIT)
- ring: declared `Apache-2.0 AND ISC`; its own code is under ISC and the
  code it took from BoringSSL under Apache-2.0 or ISC, each file saying
  which (see ring's entries)
- zstd-sys: zstd (BSD-3-Clause; also offered under GPL-2.0, which is not
  the licence ranikust uses)

